  "body": "## What changed\n\nMain was red in the app suites of the post-merge gate (run 43723593734). This PR repairs the two stale tests. No production code changed.\n\n1. `crates/app/tests/docs_troubleshooting.rs`: the test now reads `site/content/guide/reference/troubleshooting.md`. PR #1908 (commit 89b43e04d) moved the page there by design. No other file refers to the old path.\n2. `crates/app/tests/operations.rs`, `threaded_batch_matches_the_serial_loop_bit_for_bit`: the box stock is now 60 x 60 x 5, not 60 x 60 x 20.\n\n## Cause of failure 2\n\nThe panic text on main (d1484f02a):\n\n```\nAPocket3D: invalid machining parameters: 3D Pocket cannot prove shank clearance for tool 'BN-0600': Bottom of Part Z is 20.000 mm below the material top, but its wider shank starts 15.000 mm above the tip.\n```\n\nThe refusal from #1895 (#1844) is correct for that fixture:\n\n- The stock top was Z 20. The pocket top is Z 5, and Bottom Z is 0.\n- No operation ahead of the pocket removes the stock from Z 5 to Z 20.\n- The catalog BN-0600 has a 15 mm flute and an 8 mm shank (the ball is 6 mm). At Bottom Z 0 the shank is in uncut stock from Z 15 to Z 20.\n\nThe test proves that the threaded batch and the serial loop write the same bytes. It does not need deep stock. The stock now stands to the top of the cube, as the sibling test `the_shell_switch_sends_the_pocket_to_the_offset_engine` does since #96. The reach law is not changed. The decision is in `docs/decisions/1924-red-main-app-tests.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Before (main d1484f02a): `threaded_batch_matches_the_serial_loop_bit_for_bit` FAIL with the panic above.\n- After: `docs_troubleshooting::troubleshooting_messages_still_exist_in_the_sources` ok.\n- After: the whole `operations` binary: 120 passed, 0 failed, 6 ignored.\n- After: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `docs_troubleshooting::troubleshooting_messages_still_exist_in_the_sources`\n- `operations::threaded_batch_matches_the_serial_loop_bit_for_bit`\n\n## Not run\n\n- The full quick gate and the other app binaries. Only the two touched binaries changed.\n- The ignored heavy lanes of `operations`.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1924\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
